{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116220",
      "title": "Signals vs Observables",
      "lectureOrder": 213,
      "videoOrder": 204,
      "sourceHash": "d14a719a231fc0f9b09289253ee85c72f0c67e218feca81b29787bf30dc513cb",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 4.44,
          "en": "So if you compare signals to observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 6.6,
          "en": "or especially subjects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.6,
          "end": 10.05,
          "en": "they might look like they're almost the same,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.05,
          "end": 15,
          "en": "and to be honest, in certain situations they kind of are.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 18.36,
          "en": "For example, when we used a subject in a service",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.36,
          "end": 22.47,
          "en": "to share some State between different Components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.47,
          "end": 25.41,
          "en": "we definitely could have used a Signal instead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.41,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "And that indeed also might be the better way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 31.71,
          "en": "Here it's just important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.71,
          "end": 34.74,
          "en": "that Angular has a long history",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.74,
          "end": 38.22,
          "en": "and Signals are a relatively new feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.22,
          "end": 42.54,
          "en": "That's why in the past RxJS kind of had to be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.54,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "for sharing data like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 47.04,
          "en": "and for managing subscriptions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.04,
          "end": 50.82,
          "en": "With Signals, you don't necessarily need RxJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.82,
          "end": 53.37,
          "en": "for situations like this anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.37,
          "end": 55.2,
          "en": "It can still be helpful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.2,
          "end": 57.9,
          "en": "for other kinds of situations though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.9,
          "end": 61.23,
          "en": "Basically whenever you have some data source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.23,
          "end": 63.33,
          "en": "that's producing data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.33,
          "end": 66.69,
          "en": "like that interval use case I had before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.69,
          "end": 68.58,
          "en": "In such a situation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.58,
          "end": 72,
          "en": "you could absolutely also set up an interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72,
          "end": 74.65,
          "en": "with the built-in setInterval function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.53999999999999,
          "end": 78.6,
          "en": "and fire it every second like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.6,
          "end": 81.09,
          "en": "and then update some Signal in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.09,
          "end": 82.38,
          "en": "You could do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.38,
          "end": 87.03,
          "en": "but this here would arguably be less code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.03,
          "end": 89.7,
          "en": "than doing it like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.7,
          "end": 94.59,
          "en": "because the equivalent would essentially be to also set up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.59,
          "end": 97.38,
          "en": "that interval property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 97.38,
          "end": 99.39,
          "en": "which has some initial value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 99.39,
          "end": 101.31,
          "en": "which is another important difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.31,
          "end": 102.63,
          "en": "to which I'll get back.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 102.63,
          "end": 106.11,
          "en": "Signals have initial values, observables don't,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.11,
          "end": 108.42,
          "en": "but let's ignore that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.42,
          "end": 110.40299999999999,
          "en": "We can set up an initial value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.36,
          "end": 115.44,
          "en": "And then in setInterval we can set the interval Signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.44,
          "end": 119.52000000000001,
          "en": "and update it and get the previous interval number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.52000000000001,
          "end": 123.483,
          "en": "and return that number plus 1, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.31,
          "end": 128.37,
          "en": "And if we then wanted to map that emitted value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.37,
          "end": 129.9,
          "en": "to some average value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.9,
          "end": 130.89,
          "en": "we would do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.89,
          "end": 134.013,
          "en": "by setting up a computed Signal here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.94,
          "end": 136.74,
          "en": "So the doubleInterval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.74,
          "end": 141.093,
          "en": "would be the computed function being executed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.99,
          "end": 145.023,
          "en": "and that's a function imported from Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.01,
          "end": 148.11,
          "en": "And we would pass a function to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.11,
          "end": 151.53300000000002,
          "en": "and in there output this.interval times 2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 153.72,
          "end": 156.753,
          "en": "and we need to read this interval Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.62,
          "end": 159.72,
          "en": "And just as with Effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 159.72,
          "end": 161.4,
          "en": "Angular would recognize",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.4,
          "end": 163.14,
          "en": "that we're using a Signal in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.14,
          "end": 165.36,
          "en": "and it would recompute that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.36,
          "end": 168.54,
          "en": "and update this double interval property here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.54,
          "end": 170.463,
          "en": "whenever the interval changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.54,
          "end": 172.8,
          "en": "But of course, as you can tell,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 172.8,
          "end": 175.86,
          "en": "this arguably is a bit more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 175.86,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "and more work than using the interval RxJS function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 181.32,
          "en": "and pipe, and map.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 181.32,
          "end": 183.84,
          "en": "There we had it all in one place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.84,
          "end": 187.83,
          "en": "and we only needed one or two lines of code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 187.83,
          "end": 189.51,
          "en": "Here with Signals,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "we're instead managing multiple Signals",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 193.89,
          "en": "and we have to manage the interval",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.89,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "manually like this with setInterval,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.2,
          "en": "and I'm not even performing cleanup here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.2,
          "end": 201.36,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.36,
          "end": 204.93,
          "en": "In addition, this interval will also always start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.93,
          "end": 206.79,
          "en": "no matter if we are using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 206.79,
          "end": 210.48,
          "en": "that Signal value anywhere in the app or not.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 210.48,
          "end": 213,
          "en": "Whereas with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 213,
          "end": 214.86,
          "en": "those really only start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "once you have at least one subscriber.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 221.76,
          "en": "So these are some differences which might not matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.76,
          "end": 223.71,
          "en": "but which also might matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 223.71,
          "end": 226.47,
          "en": "And that's why you have both approaches",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.47,
          "end": 231.47,
          "en": "and why you can use both approaches in different situations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 231.93,
          "end": 234.51,
          "en": "But in the end, the main difference",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 234.51,
          "end": 239.34,
          "en": "is that observables in the end are values over time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.34,
          "end": 243.813,
          "en": "It's a pipeline of values that are emitted over time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 244.74,
          "end": 249.74,
          "en": "whereas Signals in the end are value containers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.84,
          "end": 254.19,
          "en": "Yes, you can change the values in those containers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 254.19,
          "end": 257.58,
          "en": "and any subscribers then will be notified,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.58,
          "end": 261.15,
          "en": "but you can also look into the container at any time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 261.15,
          "end": 265.65,
          "en": "You can read the value from a Signal at any point in time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 265.65,
          "end": 269.04,
          "en": "You can read it without setting up a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 269.04,
          "end": 269.97,
          "en": "That's optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.97,
          "end": 272.1,
          "en": "It's just done automatically for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.1,
          "end": 274.38,
          "en": "if you read a Signal in a template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.38,
          "end": 277.26,
          "en": "or in an Effect, or a computed function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 277.26,
          "end": 280.47,
          "en": "But anywhere else, you just read a value once.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.47,
          "end": 282.42,
          "en": "Whereas with observables,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 286.68,
          "en": "you have that stream of data to which you must subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.68,
          "end": 290.1,
          "en": "in order to get notified about values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 290.1,
          "end": 291.99,
          "en": "And if you do subscribe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 291.99,
          "end": 294.93,
          "en": "you also don't get a value automatically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 294.93,
          "end": 297.57,
          "en": "you'll just get it once it's there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 297.57,
          "end": 301.65,
          "en": "And that makes observables really good for events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.65,
          "end": 303.93,
          "en": "or anything like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 303.93,
          "end": 308.93,
          "en": "where values do arrive asynchronously over time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 309.39,
          "end": 312.33,
          "en": "Whereas Signals can be really awesome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 312.33,
          "end": 314.91,
          "en": "for managing application State.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 314.91,
          "end": 318.42,
          "en": "So data which is set to some initial value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 318.42,
          "end": 321.06,
          "en": "and which then may change over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 321.06,
          "end": 324.933,
          "en": "and where those changes should then be reflected in the UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.1,
          "end": 328.59,
          "en": "Ultimately, it of course also comes down",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 328.59,
          "end": 330.39,
          "en": "to your personal preferences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 330.39,
          "end": 332.46,
          "en": "to the project you are working on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.46,
          "end": 334.59000000000003,
          "en": "And it's also definitely true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 334.59000000000003,
          "end": 337.32,
          "en": "that certain problems you might be facing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 337.32,
          "end": 340.23,
          "en": "can be solved with either an observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 340.23,
          "end": 342.96,
          "en": "or a subject, or a Signal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 342.96,
          "end": 345.65999999999997,
          "en": "In addition, it's all important to note",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 345.65999999999997,
          "end": 348.03,
          "en": "that Angular gives you some tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 348.03,
          "end": 351.24,
          "en": "for converting from one world to the other.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 351.24,
          "end": 355.98,
          "en": "So for converting an observable to a Signal and vice versa,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 355.98,
          "end": 358.533,
          "en": "and that's what we'll explore next.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
